            <div xml:id="d719">

                <pb facs="0912" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.516/138: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bailly-Blanchard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-16T11:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 16,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:44
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>39. My 37, June 12, 9 a.m. From McIlhenny:</p>
                <p>Since my cable, attitude of Haitian Government has changed. Now refuses to accept
                    modifications of charter.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d719-f1"/> For this and other
                    reasons I have temporarily suspended discussion of budget.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d719-f1" n="62" xml:id="d719-f1-content">
                <p>See letter of the Financial Adviser of Haiti to the Chief of the Division of
                    Latin American Affairs, Department of State, July 21, <ref target="#pg762">p.
                        762</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
